  ("A review and meta-analysis of methodological and subject variables influencing the exposure-affect" 0.2087 0.7888 0.2216 0.2362 0.2362 0.0146 0.00383 0.2988 0.0098 "Times-Roman" 0.0111 nil nil 0)
  ("relationship was performed on studies of the mere exposure effect published in the 20 years following" 0.2087 0.7894 0.2346 0.2491 0.2491 0.0146 0.00381 0.3501 0.0690 "Times-Roman" 0.0112 nil nil 0)
  ("Zajonc's (1968)-seminal monograph. Stimulus type, stimulus complexity, presentation sequence," 0.2087 0.7900 0.2472 0.2618 0.2618 0.0146 0.00391 0.3136 0.0492 "Times-Roman" 0.0112 nil nil 0)
