  ("An extensive literature search of Psychological Abstracts was" 0.0850 0.4843 0.1672 0.1835 0.1835 0.0163 0.0041 0.2923 0.0198 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0)
  ("conducted to obtain references for studies of mere exposure" 0.0700 0.4843 0.1814 0.1977 0.1977 0.0163 0.00437 0.2230 0.0678 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("effects in human subjects published between 1968 and 1987. In" 0.0696 0.4838 0.1953 0.2115 0.2115 0.0163 0.00426 0.3000 0.0398 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0)
  ("addition, a computer search using the PsychlNFO data base" 0.0700 0.4843 0.2095 0.2257 0.2257 0.0163 0.00437 0.2590 0.0577 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("was performed to obtain any published articles that had not" 0.0696 0.4833 0.2236 0.2399 0.2399 0.0163 0.00437 0.2560 0.0251 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0)
  ("been included in Psychological Abstracts. The following key" 0.0696 0.4834 0.2375 0.2538 0.2538 0.0163 0.00417 0.2396 0.0308 "Times-Italic" 0.0119 nil t 0)
  ("words were used to search Psychological Abstracts and Psych-" 0.0696 0.4834 0.2517 0.2680 0.2680 0.0163 0.00425 0.2556 0.0402 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("lNFO: mere exposure, exposure effects, exposure-affect, famil-" 0.0696 0.4839 0.2668 0.2818 0.2818 0.0149 0.004 0.3872 0.0425 "Times-Italic" 0.0121 nil t 0)
  ("iarity-affect, familiarity effects, stimulus frequency-affect, stim-" 0.0704 0.4851 0.2810 0.2959 0.2959 0.0149 0.00413 0.4459 0.0685 "Times-Italic" 0.0114 nil t 0)
  ("ulus duration-affect, stimulus complexity-affect, stimulus inter-" 0.0704 0.4839 0.2949 0.3098 0.3098 0.0149 0.00395 0.4190 0.0279 "Times-Italic" 0.0115 nil t 0)
  ("val-affect," 0.0704 0.1236 0.3091 0.3240 0.3240 0.0149 0.00345 0.2600 0.0532 "Times-Italic" 0.0109 nil t 0)
  ("novelty-affect," 0.1433 0.2218 0.3091 0.3240 0.3240 0.0149 0.0038 0.2498 0.0785 "Times-Italic" 0.0112 nil t 0)
  ("and novelty effects." 0.2433 0.3689 0.3079 0.3241 0.3241 0.0149 0.0038 0.3908 0.0216 "Times-Italic" 0.0118 nil t 0)
  ("All published" 0.3883 0.4829 0.3079 0.3241 0.3241 0.0163 0.00437 0.3445 0.0191 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("studies of the exposure-affect relationship conducted between" 0.0696 0.4830 0.3217 0.3380 0.3380 0.0163 0.00437 0.2423 0.0442 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("1968 and 1987 that were cited in these articles were also in-" 0.0717 0.4836 0.3359 0.3522 0.3522 0.0163 0.00437 0.2954 0.0232 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("cluded. The only inclusion criteria for studies (discussed in de-" 0.0696 0.4836 0.3498 0.3661 0.3661 0.0163 0.00437 0.2795 0.0480 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("tail earlier) were that (a) they were conducted on human sub-" 0.0692 0.4836 0.3640 0.3803 0.3803 0.0163 0.00437 0.3079 0.0209 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("jects; (b) they were studies of unreinforced exposure to visual" 0.0675 0.4829 0.3779 0.3942 0.3942 0.0163 0.00437 0.2617 0.0358 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0)
  ("or auditory stimuli; and (c) they involved some dependent mea-" 0.0696 0.4836 0.3921 0.4084 0.4084 0.0163 0.00437 0.3683 0.0140 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("sure of affect after stimulus exposures. Overall, 134 published" 0.0692 0.4829 0.4063 0.4226 0.4226 0.0163 0.00437 0.2794 0.0281 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("articles reporting a total of 208 independent effect sizes were" 0.0696 0.4834 0.4205 0.4368 0.4368 0.0163 0.00437 0.2565 0.0468 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("included in the meta-analysis." 0.0692 0.2654 0.4343 0.4506 0.4506 0.0163 0.00429 0.3107 0.0575 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("Following Rosenthal (1984), I used the product-moment cor-" 0.0846 0.4832 0.4482 0.4645 0.4645 0.0163 0.00437 0.3468 0.0645 "Times-Roman" 0.0128 nil nil 0)
  ("relation coefficient (r) as the effect-size estimate for meta-analy-" 0.0700 0.4840 0.4624 0.4787 0.4787 0.0163 0.00409 0.3089 0.0505 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0)
  ("sis. The correlation coefficient r was chosen as the effect-size" 0.0696 0.4834 0.4763 0.4926 0.4926 0.0163 0.00428 0.2550 0.0196 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0)
  ("estimate because studies of the exposure effect typically assess" 0.0696 0.4844 0.4905 0.5068 0.5068 0.0163 0.00437 0.2601 0.0553 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("the relationship between two continuous variables (number of" 0.0696 0.4828 0.5044 0.5206 0.5206 0.0163 0.00437 0.3175 0.0203 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("stimulus exposures and an affect rating of the stimulus), so that" 0.0696 0.4833 0.5186 0.5349 0.5349 0.0163 0.00428 0.3432 0.0568 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("r seemed the most easily comprehensible representation of the" 0.0700 0.4842 0.5324 0.5487 0.5487 0.0163 0.00437 0.3066 0.0063 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("magnitude of the exposure-affect relationship. Combined (av-" 0.0696 0.4836 0.5466 0.5629 0.5629 0.0163 0.00437 0.2994 0.0709 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("erage) effect sizes were computed by transforming each r into a" 0.0696 0.4834 0.5608 0.5771 0.5771 0.0163 0.00424 0.3363 0.0403 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("Fisher's z coefficient, obtaining the sum of the Fisher's zs, divid-" 0.0696 0.4836 0.5747 0.5910 0.5910 0.0163 0.00432 0.3569 0.0511 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
  ("ing each sum by the number of studies used to obtain it, and" 0.0696 0.4829 0.5889 0.6052 0.6052 0.0163 0.00435 0.2981 0.0207 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0)
  ("converting the resulting z back into an r (Rosenthal, 1984). The" 0.0696 0.4834 0.6028 0.6191 0.6191 0.0163 0.00429 0.3319 0.0703 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0)
  ("Stouffer method of adding standard normal deviate zs (Mos-" 0.0696 0.4836 0.6170 0.6332 0.6332 0.0163 0.00437 0.3000 0.0500 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0)
